    "field": "Phylogeography",
    "problem": "Recovering species' demographic histories is challenging because defining biologically plausible and spatially explicit scenarios of past range dynamics for coalescent modeling often lacks independent, non-genetic evidence to test competing hypotheses.",
    "method": "The paper proposes a method to recover a species' demographical history by coupling ecological niche modeling to generate past distribution hypotheses with coalescent simulations of genetic data to test these competing demographic scenarios.",
    "task": "The task is to recover the demographic history and past distribution of the Brazilian Cerrado tree species *Caryocar brasiliense* by coupling ecological niche modeling with coalescent-based genetic analyses to understand its response to Quaternary climate changes.",
